Patch 53 -- resolve the island's GL slots by name, not by address.

The ARM island calls GL through gl_info->gl_ops, which holds guest x86 pointers.
Patch 51 translated that table once by matching each pointer's address against
opengl32.dll's export table. That approach cannot work, and failed twice:

  * the RVA table was generated from the reference wineprefix's opengl32.dll
    rather than the one MOUNTED on the device. Same ImageBase, different build
    -- 1.8 MB vs 4.9 MB, 380 vs 391 exports. 3 of 493 slots resolved.
  * regenerating from the device's own DLL raised that to 88, and 88 is the
    ceiling: the extension entry points are not exports at all. They are
    internal thunks Wine's opengl32 builds for wglGetProcAddress, so no export
    table can ever name them.

Unresolved slots were written back as NULL, so the first genuine GL_EXTCALL
through one dereferenced NULL -- in-game, minutes after load, far from the cause.

The address was the wrong key. gl_ops is generated on both sides from the same
macro lists (ALL_WGL_FUNCS, ALL_GL_FUNCS, ALL_WGL_EXT_FUNCS, ALL_GL_EXT_FUNCS),
so a slot's POSITION already carries its name, by construction, with nothing to
look up and nothing to go stale. This patch expands those lists in declaration
order into mgs2_gl_slot_name[] and resolves each live slot by name against the
already-loaded driver (box86's mgs2_island_gl_by_name: dlsym, then
eglGetProcAddress). The address path stays as a fallback.

A C_ASSERT ties the array length to sizeof(struct wined3d_gl_funcs) /
sizeof(void *). If the names ever shift against the slots, every GL call would
go to the wrong function -- the same silent mis-aim as a stale class-B table --
so that has to fail the build, not the run.

Measured on the device: 3 -> 88 -> 233 of 493 non-null slots resolved, and the
routed island reaches in-game frames with zero faults. The remaining 260 are not
reached on this path and stay NULL with a report.

--- a/dlls/wined3d/utils.c
+++ b/dlls/wined3d/utils.c
@@ -7538,10 +7538,36 @@
  * one adapter; a second would simply re-translate, which is correct if slower.
  */
 void *mgs2_island_try_resolve(void *fp);
+void *mgs2_island_gl_by_name(const char *name);
 void mgs2_island_report_unresolved(unsigned int slot, void *fp);
 void mgs2_island_report_gl_info(unsigned int total, unsigned int null_in,
         unsigned int resolved, unsigned int failed);
 
+/*
+ * Slot index -> GL function name, in the exact order gl_ops declares them.
+ *
+ * The first attempt matched each pointer's address against opengl32.dll's
+ * export table. That was wrong twice over. It resolved 3 of 493 while the table
+ * came from the reference wineprefix rather than the DLL actually mounted, and
+ * even against the right DLL it only reached 88: the extension entries are not
+ * exports at all, they are internal thunks Wine's opengl32 builds for
+ * wglGetProcAddress, so no export table can ever name them.
+ *
+ * Addresses were the wrong key. The struct is generated from these same macro
+ * lists on both sides, so the slot's POSITION already carries its name -- by
+ * construction, with no table to go stale and nothing to match against. Expand
+ * the lists in declaration order and the index is the name.
+ */
+static const char *const mgs2_gl_slot_name[] =
+{
+#define USE_GL_FUNC(x) #x,
+    ALL_WGL_FUNCS
+    ALL_GL_FUNCS
+    ALL_WGL_EXT_FUNCS
+    ALL_GL_EXT_FUNCS
+#undef USE_GL_FUNC
+};
+
 const struct wined3d_gl_info *mgs2_island_gl_info(const struct wined3d_gl_info *guest)
 {
     static struct wined3d_gl_info translated;
@@ -7557,6 +7583,11 @@
     translated = *guest;
     slot = (void **)&translated.gl_ops;
     count = sizeof(translated.gl_ops) / sizeof(void *);
+    /* If these ever disagree the names have silently shifted against the slots,
+     * and every GL call would go to the wrong function -- the same silent
+     * mis-aim as the stale class-B table. Fail the build, not the run. */
+    C_ASSERT(sizeof(mgs2_gl_slot_name) / sizeof(mgs2_gl_slot_name[0])
+            == sizeof(struct wined3d_gl_funcs) / sizeof(void *));
     {
         /* Report the whole table at once. Chasing one unresolved pointer per
          * device run costs ten minutes each; this names every gap in a single
@@ -7568,7 +7599,12 @@
             void *before = slot[i];
 
             if (!before) { ++null_in; continue; }
-            slot[i] = mgs2_island_try_resolve(before);
+            /* By name first: it is the key that cannot go stale. The address
+             * path stays as a fallback for anything the driver exposes under a
+             * different name than wined3d's slot. */
+            slot[i] = mgs2_island_gl_by_name(mgs2_gl_slot_name[i]);
+            if (!slot[i])
+                slot[i] = mgs2_island_try_resolve(before);
             if (slot[i]) ++ok;
             else { ++failed; mgs2_island_report_unresolved((unsigned int)i, before); }
         }
